10:31:11.833 | The rumble of burdened caravan wheels carries across the area. Crackling ozone heralds warp-touched mirage, their coming the advent of change. Sand has covered the location. Vines have overtaken this location. A wall of celadon-tinged fog deluges the surroundings in the sickly scent of stale water. The trunk of a massive fallen tree floats lopsidedly in the stagnant water of the bog here, slowly decomposing into the thick mud surrounding it. Broad patches of fungus grow across its surface, and deep, twisting lines in the wood testify to the presence of some voracious insect or worm. Small ripples occasionally shimmer across the surface of the water near the floating trunk, as tiny fish dart around its decaying corpse. A faint mist hovers in the air, carrying with it a vaguely repugnant scent. A symmetrical leather tent is constructed here, providing shelter against the elements. Inverted wings pointed skyward, Lethe, a great white bat considers her dominion. Like a mountain against the wind, a storm bull is standing here, motionless. A Baalzadeen demon towers over you, filling you with dread. There are 2 daemonic hyenas here. Hands of rotting flesh and white bone push up from the ground. The surroundings are distorted, as if viewed through water. Ethereal mist traces a pale echo of days past and times forgotten. Tomekeeper Harkon d'Ivoire, Scourge of His Legion is here. He wields a leaf-bladed ritual knife in his left hand. Havyn d'Ivoire is riding on a storm bull. She wields a Shield of Absorption in her left hand. Director Nagis Lichlord, Squire of Mhaldor is here. His features are obscured by a charred and torn leather-muzzled mask. He wields a Scimitar of Eagles in each hand. Sir Antoninus Nithilar is here. He wields a vorpal sword in his left hand and Matsuhama's morningstar in his right. Sir Arador Aristata, Knight of Mhaldor is here. He wields a Scimitar of Eagles in each hand. The Golden Dragon Sprucebruce's imposing form looms.
10:31:11.833 | You see a single exit leading south.
