10:33:15.182 | Entering a gloomy bog.
10:33:15.182 | The rumble of burdened caravan wheels carries across the area. Crackling ozone heralds warp-touched mirage, their coming the advent of change. A wall of celadon-tinged fog deluges the surroundings in the sickly scent of stale water. The heavy scent of decaying vegetation fills this area with an almost overwhelming miasma, hovering in the stagnant air beneath the overhanging mangrove trees. Thick muck and peat layer the ground, making passage difficult and treacherous, and long grass grows up in ragged patches around the bases of the larger trees. The air opens up to the northwest, where the open space of the Prelatorian Highway is barely visible, while the dark gloom of the bog to the south offers a threatening contrast to the road's welcoming smoothness. Stretching its wings in an impressive display is an ebony pegasus, its dark coat absorbing the surrounding light. A massive creature of rock and earth sits immobile as a stone. Smoke and fire churns heavily upon the hulking frame of an ashbeast. An icewall is here, blocking passage to the west. Dunn Lichlord, Avatar of Ruin is riding on an ebony pegasus. His features are obscured by a rotting mask of mangrove wood and swamp debris. He wields a knurled mangrove staff in his left hand and a spearhead-tipped dirk bound to a mangrove hilt in his right. Sir Antoninus Nithilar is here. He wields a Braincrusher flail in each hand. The Golden Dragon Sprucebruce's imposing form looms.
